  "goodToKnow": "Die Wasserkraft is hydropower: Strom aus Wasserkraft, das Wasserkraftwerk. In Germany, it supplies only a few percent of electricity, mostly from rivers in Bavaria and Baden-Württemberg, as the country is relatively flat. In Austria, Switzerland and Norway it dominates. Pumped-storage plants (Pumpspeicherkraftwerke) store energy. Die Kraft means power. It has no plural."
